1
00:00:00,990 --> 00:00:06,930
Zankoku na tenshi no you ni

2
00:00:00,990 --> 00:00:06,930
Just like the cruel angel

3
00:00:06,930 --> 00:00:14,590
Shounen yo shinwa ni nare

4
00:00:06,930 --> 00:00:14,590
Young boy, become a legend

5
00:00:18,990 --> 00:00:22,410
2D4U PRESENTS:

6
00:00:22,770 --> 00:00:25,810
Aoi kaze ga ima

7
00:00:22,770 --> 00:00:25,810
Even though the untested breeze...

8
00:00:25,810 --> 00:00:29,510
mune no doa o tataitemo

9
00:00:25,810 --> 00:00:29,510
...taps at the door to your heart

10
00:00:29,510 --> 00:00:36,970
Watashi dake o tada mitsumete hohoenderu anata

11
00:00:29,510 --> 00:00:36,970
You just look solely at me and smile

12
00:00:37,560 --> 00:00:44,500
Sotto fureru mono motomeru koto ni muchuu de

13
00:00:37,560 --> 00:00:44,500
So intent on seeking out that gentle touch

14
00:00:44,500 --> 00:00:51,400
Unmei sae mada shiranai itaike na hitomi

15
00:00:44,500 --> 00:00:51,400
Such innocent eyes, still ignorant of their destiny

16
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:55,750
Dakedo itsuka kizuku deshou

17
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:55,750
But someday, you are sure to realize...

18
00:00:55,750 --> 00:00:58,340
sono senaka ni wa

19
00:00:55,750 --> 00:00:58,340
...that upon your back

20
00:00:59,510 --> 00:01:02,960
Haruka mirai mezasu tame

21
00:00:59,510 --> 00:01:02,960
You have the wings with which to fly...

22
00:01:02,960 --> 00:01:06,310
no hane ga aru koto

23
00:01:02,960 --> 00:01:06,310
...towards the distant future

24
00:01:06,990 --> 00:01:10,690
Zankoku na tenshi no teeze

25
00:01:06,990 --> 00:01:10,690
The cruel angel's thesis

26
00:01:10,690 --> 00:01:14,430
Madobe kara yagate tobidatsu

27
00:01:10,690 --> 00:01:14,430
Soon, you will take flight from the windowsill

28
00:01:14,430 --> 00:01:18,200
Hotobashiru atsui patosu de

29
00:01:14,430 --> 00:01:18,200
With your torrent of ardent pathos

30
00:01:18,200 --> 00:01:21,900
Omoide o uragiru nara

31
00:01:18,200 --> 00:01:21,900
If you are to betray our memories

32
00:01:21,900 --> 00:01:25,540
Kono sora o daite kagayaku

33
00:01:21,900 --> 00:01:25,540
You, who embrace these heavens and shine

34
00:01:25,540 --> 00:01:29,270
Shounen yo shinwa ni nare

35
00:01:25,540 --> 00:01:29,270
Young boy, become a legend

36
00:01:31,900 --> 00:01:36,450
Correct, I have already arranged it
with the committee.

37
00:01:36,450 --> 00:01:38,950
The cargo left from Sasebo Port yesterday,

38
00:01:38,950 --> 00:01:40,830
and is now making its way here
across the Pacific Ocean.

39
00:01:44,410 --> 00:01:47,120
A MIG-55 D transport helicopter!

40
00:01:47,120 --> 00:01:50,790
I'd never have had the chance to fly in one
if it weren't for something like this.

41
00:01:50,790 --> 00:01:54,670
Man, this is what friends are for, right, Shinji?

42
00:01:55,510 --> 00:01:59,180
I figured you'd get claustrophobic looking at
the same mountains day after day,

43
00:01:59,180 --> 00:02:02,310
so I invited you on a date,
since it is a Sunday.

44
00:02:02,310 --> 00:02:06,430
What?! Then today is a real date?

45
00:02:06,430 --> 00:02:11,110
I bought this cap just for today, Miss Misato!

46
00:02:11,110 --> 00:02:13,020
So, where are we headed?

47
00:02:13,020 --> 00:02:16,030
We're taking a little jaunt across the Pacific
on a gorgeous cruise ship.

48
00:02:18,860 --> 00:02:23,120
Wow! Five aircraft carriers and
four battleships! What a fleet!

49
00:02:23,120 --> 00:02:26,080
This really IS what friends are for!

50
00:02:26,080 --> 00:02:28,210
That's your gorgeous cruise ship?

51
00:02:28,210 --> 00:02:29,540
Yeah, she sure is gorgeous!

52
00:02:29,540 --> 00:02:31,670
That's the pride of the U.N.,
the glorious regular carrier

53
00:02:31,670 --> 00:02:33,500
"Over the Rainbow"!

54
00:02:33,670 --> 00:02:34,920
It's huge.

55
00:02:35,000 --> 00:02:38,010
I'm surprised that such a relic is still afloat.

56
00:02:38,170 --> 00:02:39,470
Nah, it's not so bad.

57
00:02:39,470 --> 00:02:42,640
It's a vintage model from before
the Second lmpact.

58
00:02:43,550 --> 00:02:46,310
Give me a break!

59
00:02:46,310 --> 00:02:49,140
Here comes the socket for that kid's toy.

60
00:02:49,140 --> 00:02:50,230
What a child's errand!

61
00:03:00,910 --> 00:03:02,370
Awesome! Awesome!

62
00:03:02,370 --> 00:03:03,660
Awesome! Awesome!

63
00:03:03,660 --> 00:03:05,700
Awesome! Awesome! Awesome!

64
00:03:05,700 --> 00:03:06,830
This is way too awesome!

65
00:03:06,830 --> 00:03:10,040
Real men shed tears for this kind of thing!

66
00:03:10,710 --> 00:03:14,790
Awesome! Awesome! Awesome!
Awesome! Awesome!

67
00:03:14,790 --> 00:03:17,130
Hey, wait! Wait up!

68
00:03:21,720 --> 00:03:23,930
Damn it!

69
00:03:23,930 --> 00:03:25,510
Stop! Stop already!

70
00:03:29,730 --> 00:03:31,560
Hello, Misato.

71
00:03:31,560 --> 00:03:33,860
How have you been?

72
00:03:33,860 --> 00:03:36,650
Fine. How about you?
You've grown some, haven't you?

73
00:03:36,650 --> 00:03:41,200
Yeah! I'm not just taller,
my figure's filled out as well.

74
00:03:41,200 --> 00:03:42,570
Let me introduce you.

75
00:03:42,570 --> 00:03:46,950
This is the pilot of Evangelion Unit 02,
the Second Child,

76
00:03:46,950 --> 00:03:49,040
Asuka Langley Sohryu.

77
00:03:51,330 --> 00:03:53,460
Episode 8

78
00:03:51,830 --> 00:03:53,460
Asuka

79
00:03:52,330 --> 00:03:53,460
Arrives in Japan

80
00:03:53,670 --> 00:03:55,380
What did you do that for?!

81
00:03:57,090 --> 00:03:59,710
That's the viewing fee.
Quite a bargain, don't you think?

82
00:03:59,710 --> 00:04:03,430
What? Well then, take a look at this!

83
00:04:05,220 --> 00:04:06,930
What the hell are you doing?!

84
00:04:08,470 --> 00:04:11,930
So, which one is the famous Third Child?

85
00:04:11,930 --> 00:04:13,850
Don't tell me that was him.

86
00:04:13,850 --> 00:04:16,980
No, it's him.

87
00:04:16,980 --> 00:04:20,190
Well, he looks kind of dull.

88
00:04:20,190 --> 00:04:24,780
Well, well, I thought you were the leader
of this gang of Boy Scouts,

89
00:04:24,780 --> 00:04:28,200
but it seems I was mistaken.

90
00:04:28,200 --> 00:04:31,500
Thank you for your understanding, Captain.

91
00:04:31,500 --> 00:04:37,340
Oh no, thank you for giving me the
opportunity to baby-sit some kids.

92
00:04:37,340 --> 00:04:42,050
We appreciate your assistance
in the transport of Unit 02.

93
00:04:42,050 --> 00:04:44,720
Here are the specs for the
emergency power supply socket.

94
00:04:46,180 --> 00:04:51,390
In the first place, I haven't heard anything
about activating that toy while at sea.

95
00:04:51,390 --> 00:04:55,980
Why don't you just think of this as
being prepared for an emergency?

96
00:04:55,980 --> 00:05:01,190
That's why the Pacific Fleet is escorting it.

97
00:05:01,190 --> 00:05:05,280
When did the UN Navy
become a cargo service?

98
00:05:05,280 --> 00:05:09,450
It believe it was just after a certain
organization was established.

99
00:05:09,450 --> 00:05:12,540
Quite a grandiose escort for
transporting one single toy!

100
00:05:12,540 --> 00:05:14,870
After all, this is the entire Pacific Fleet.

101
00:05:14,870 --> 00:05:18,580
It's still not enough, considering
the importance of the Eva.

102
00:05:18,580 --> 00:05:20,380
Would you sign this document?

103
00:05:20,380 --> 00:05:23,710
Not yet. Eva Unit 02 and its pilot
have been entrusted to us

104
00:05:23,710 --> 00:05:26,680
by the Third Branch in Germany.

105
00:05:26,680 --> 00:05:28,890
You can't just do as you please!

106
00:05:28,890 --> 00:05:30,760
Then, when will you transfer them to us?

107
00:05:30,760 --> 00:05:33,560
Once we've unloaded in New Yokosuka.

108
00:05:33,560 --> 00:05:36,310
The ocean is our jurisdiction.

109
00:05:36,310 --> 00:05:38,230
You will follow our orders here.

110
00:05:38,230 --> 00:05:39,860
I understand.

111
00:05:39,860 --> 00:05:42,820
However, I should remind you that,
in the case of an emergency,

112
00:05:42,820 --> 00:05:45,610
Nerv's authority overrides yours.

113
00:05:45,610 --> 00:05:47,280
She's cool!

114
00:05:47,280 --> 00:05:48,820
She's practically like Miss Ritsuko.

115
00:05:48,820 --> 00:05:51,370
You're as gallant as ever.

116
00:05:51,370 --> 00:05:52,540
Kaji!

117
00:05:54,750 --> 00:05:58,000
Mr. Kaji, I don't recall inviting you
onto the bridge.

118
00:05:58,000 --> 00:05:59,750
Oh, sorry about that.

119
00:05:59,750 --> 00:06:04,840
Excuse us, then. We're counting on you to
escort us to New Yokosuka as ordered.

120
00:06:00,750 --> 00:06:03,090
This is a date?

121
00:06:03,090 --> 00:06:04,840
Awesome! Too awesome!

122
00:06:04,840 --> 00:06:08,550
Shit! Those kids are really going
to save the Earth?

123
00:06:08,550 --> 00:06:10,720
Times are changing.

124
00:06:10,720 --> 00:06:13,970
I understand that Congress has also
pinned its hopes on that robot.

125
00:06:13,970 --> 00:06:17,560
On that toy? The idiots!

126
00:06:17,560 --> 00:06:21,230
If they've got the money for it,
they should give it to us!

127
00:06:25,190 --> 00:06:28,650
What are you doing here?!

128
00:06:28,650 --> 00:06:30,280
Accompanying her.

129
00:06:30,280 --> 00:06:32,120
I'm on a business trip from Germany.

130
00:06:32,120 --> 00:06:36,870
Man, was I careless.
I should have anticipated this.

131
00:06:36,870 --> 00:06:38,750
Hey! Don't touch me!

132
00:06:38,750 --> 00:06:40,000
I can't help it!

133
00:06:40,000 --> 00:06:42,840
Squadron 3 will sortie as scheduled.

134
00:06:42,840 --> 00:06:45,840
Seeing anyone right now?

135
00:06:45,840 --> 00:06:48,220
And that would be your business WHY?

136
00:06:48,220 --> 00:06:51,010
What? You're kind of cold.

137
00:06:51,470 --> 00:06:54,180
I hear that you're living with Katsuragi?

138
00:06:54,180 --> 00:06:56,020
Yes.

139
00:06:56,020 --> 00:06:59,350
So, does she still toss and turn in bed?

140
00:07:01,940 --> 00:07:04,190
Wha... wha...

141
00:07:04,190 --> 00:07:06,070
What are you saying?!

142
00:07:06,900 --> 00:07:09,570
So, she hasn't changed, has she,
Mister Shinji Ikari?

143
00:07:09,570 --> 00:07:11,160
Well...

144
00:07:11,160 --> 00:07:13,620
Huh? How do you know my name?

145
00:07:13,620 --> 00:07:15,160
Well, of course I do.

146
00:07:15,160 --> 00:07:17,950
You're famous in our business.

147
00:07:17,950 --> 00:07:21,500
The Third Child, who piloted an Eva
in battle with no training.

148
00:07:22,420 --> 00:07:25,500
Oh, no, it was just luck.

149
00:07:25,500 --> 00:07:28,880
Luck is a part of your destiny. It's your talent.

150
00:07:29,760 --> 00:07:31,430
Well, I'll see you later.

151
00:07:31,430 --> 00:07:31,800
See you.

152
00:07:31,800 --> 00:07:33,720
This has got to be a bad joke.
No, a nightmare.

153
00:07:36,510 --> 00:07:38,810
So, what do you think about
Mister Shinji Ikari?

154
00:07:38,810 --> 00:07:43,650
He's boring. That's the great Third Child?
What a disappointment.

155
00:07:43,650 --> 00:07:48,190
Yet his sync ratio was well over 40%
in combat with no training.

156
00:07:48,190 --> 00:07:49,740
No way!

157
00:07:49,740 --> 00:07:52,610
That captain's attitude gets on my nerves.

158
00:07:52,610 --> 00:07:54,740
He's a proud man.

159
00:07:54,740 --> 00:07:57,410
Pride can make you sarcastic.

160
00:07:57,410 --> 00:08:00,620
That Mr. Kaji is pretty lively and funny.

161
00:08:00,620 --> 00:08:03,210
He hasn't changed at all, that jerk.

162
00:08:03,210 --> 00:08:04,380
Hey, Third Child!

163
00:08:05,790 --> 00:08:07,090
Come with me!

164
00:08:15,340 --> 00:08:18,930
So Unit 02 is red? I didn't know that.

165
00:08:18,930 --> 00:08:22,100
The color isn't the only difference.

166
00:08:22,100 --> 00:08:24,230
After all, Units 00 and 01 were created

167
00:08:24,230 --> 00:08:27,310
as part of a development process,
prototype and test type.

168
00:08:27,310 --> 00:08:32,320
The fact that it synchronized with an
untrained pilot like you is proof of that.

169
00:08:32,320 --> 00:08:34,780
But Unit 02 is different.

170
00:08:34,780 --> 00:08:36,820
Created for actual combat conditions,

171
00:08:36,820 --> 00:08:40,120
this is the world's first true Evangelion.

172
00:08:40,120 --> 00:08:41,700
This is the final model!

173
00:08:43,910 --> 00:08:45,420
What was that?

174
00:08:45,420 --> 00:08:48,090
An undersea shock wave!

175
00:08:48,090 --> 00:08:49,170
That explosion was nearby!

176
00:08:51,050 --> 00:08:51,710
What's that?

177
00:08:56,140 --> 00:08:57,850
Could it be an Angel?

178
00:08:57,850 --> 00:08:59,390
That? A real one?

179
00:09:01,470 --> 00:09:04,940
What'll we do? We have to get back
to Miss Misato.

180
00:09:07,060 --> 00:09:08,310
This is my chance!

181
00:09:13,740 --> 00:09:17,200
All ships take evasive action,
but watch the formation!

182
00:09:17,200 --> 00:09:18,780
Where's the status report?

183
00:09:18,780 --> 00:09:23,000
The Cymbeline's gone silent.
Titus Andronicus can't locate the target!

184
00:09:23,000 --> 00:09:25,710
Damn it! What in the hell is going on here?!

185
00:09:25,710 --> 00:09:27,710
Hello, Nerv calling.

186
00:09:27,710 --> 00:09:31,050
Interested in info on the unknown enemy
and the appropriate countermeasures?

187
00:09:31,050 --> 00:09:34,220
This is a combat situation!
No non-essential personnel allowed!

188
00:09:34,220 --> 00:09:37,930
This is just my opinion, but I'd say
this must be an Angel attack.

189
00:09:37,930 --> 00:09:40,010
All ships, fire at will!

190
00:09:40,010 --> 00:09:40,300
Roger.

191
00:09:40,300 --> 00:09:41,140
It's pointless.
Roger.

192
00:09:51,820 --> 00:09:55,490
So an AT field can't be penetrated
with this kind of firepower.

193
00:09:55,490 --> 00:09:58,450
But why is an Angel here?

194
00:09:58,450 --> 00:09:59,530
Could it be after Unit 02?

195
00:10:02,790 --> 00:10:04,660
Hey, where are we going?

196
00:10:06,830 --> 00:10:08,370
Just wait here a second.

197
00:10:09,580 --> 00:10:11,090
What's going on?

198
00:10:19,390 --> 00:10:21,760
Don't peep, you pervert!

199
00:10:19,840 --> 00:10:21,180
Sorry!

200
00:10:21,760 --> 00:10:24,640
Why are all boys such perverted jerks?

201
00:10:32,610 --> 00:10:34,360
Here we go, Asuka.

202
00:10:41,410 --> 00:10:42,830
Why won't it sink?!

203
00:10:42,830 --> 00:10:45,370
I knew it. Only an Eva can beat it!

204
00:10:50,920 --> 00:10:52,540
Come on, let's go.

205
00:10:53,340 --> 00:10:55,750
You're coming with me!

206
00:10:58,010 --> 00:11:01,680
Hey, why'd we change into these plug suits?

207
00:11:01,680 --> 00:11:03,050
What are you, stupid?

208
00:11:03,050 --> 00:11:06,140
What else? We're going to beat it
with my Unit 02!

209
00:11:07,680 --> 00:11:10,810
No way! Do you have permission
from Miss Misato?

210
00:11:10,810 --> 00:11:12,650
I can get permission after I've beaten it.

211
00:11:15,360 --> 00:11:19,650
Now, I'll show you how magnificent
my piloting is, up close and personal!

212
00:11:20,200 --> 00:11:22,070
Just don't disturb me.

213
00:11:27,620 --> 00:11:30,460
This is odd. It almost seems to be
looking for something.

214
00:11:31,620 --> 00:11:34,000
For an Angel to attack here...

215
00:11:34,000 --> 00:11:35,840
Isn't it a little different from the deal we had?

216
00:11:35,840 --> 00:11:37,840
This is what Unit 02 is for,

217
00:11:37,840 --> 00:11:40,170
and I've generously provided
a second pilot as a reserve.

218
00:11:41,050 --> 00:11:44,930
If worse comes to worst, escape by yourself.

219
00:11:45,680 --> 00:11:46,720
I know.

220
00:11:49,560 --> 00:11:51,850
LCL Füllung.

221
00:11:51,850 --> 00:11:54,060
Anfang der Bewegung.

222
00:11:54,060 --> 00:11:56,860
Anfang des Nervenanschlusses.

223
00:11:56,860 --> 00:11:59,940
Auslösung von Linkskleigung.

224
00:11:59,940 --> 00:12:01,570
Synchro-start.

225
00:12:05,370 --> 00:12:07,200
Program error? What happened?

226
00:12:07,200 --> 00:12:10,370
Thought noise! I told you not to disturb me.

227
00:12:10,370 --> 00:12:11,410
What do you mean?

228
00:12:11,410 --> 00:12:15,830
You're thinking in Japanese, aren't you?
Think in German.

229
00:12:15,830 --> 00:12:19,420
Oh, okay. Baumkuchen...

230
00:12:19,420 --> 00:12:25,010
Idiot! Just forget it.
Switch the base language to Japanese.

231
00:12:27,760 --> 00:12:30,310
Evangelion Unit 02, activate.

232
00:12:30,980 --> 00:12:34,020
Telex from the Othello! Unit 02 is in
the process of activation.

233
00:12:34,020 --> 00:12:35,060
What the...

234
00:12:35,060 --> 00:12:36,150
Nice going, Asuka!

235
00:12:38,980 --> 00:12:41,780
No! Abort the activation sequence!
Reset it!

236
00:12:42,440 --> 00:12:44,450
Don't worry about him, Asuka! Just launch!

237
00:12:44,450 --> 00:12:45,950
What are you saying?!

238
00:12:46,030 --> 00:12:49,950
You can't just violate my command authority
over the Eva and its pilot!

239
00:12:49,950 --> 00:12:51,790
What are you talking about?
This is an emergency!

240
00:12:51,790 --> 00:12:53,500
Who gives a damn about your procedures?

241
00:12:54,250 --> 00:12:56,000
Are you really serious?

242
00:12:56,000 --> 00:12:59,090
Unit 02 is still using type B equipment!

243
00:12:59,090 --> 00:13:01,550
Wouldn't it be bad if we fell in the sea?

244
00:13:01,550 --> 00:13:03,050
So we don't fall in.

245
00:13:03,050 --> 00:13:04,720
Shinji, are you in there too?

246
00:13:04,720 --> 00:13:05,510
Yes.

247
00:13:05,510 --> 00:13:07,140
Two kids!

248
00:13:07,140 --> 00:13:08,890
Good chance to test it...

249
00:13:08,890 --> 00:13:10,060
Asuka, launch!

250
00:13:12,680 --> 00:13:13,770
It's coming!

251
00:13:13,770 --> 00:13:14,350
Here we go!

252
00:13:22,110 --> 00:13:23,360
Where is it?

253
00:13:22,900 --> 00:13:23,530
That way!

254
00:13:25,150 --> 00:13:26,950
We've only got 58 seconds left!

255
00:13:26,950 --> 00:13:28,780
I know that! Misato!

256
00:13:28,780 --> 00:13:31,370
Get the external power supply onto the deck.

257
00:13:32,040 --> 00:13:33,160
Understood.

258
00:13:33,160 --> 00:13:34,500
What is she going to do?

259
00:13:34,500 --> 00:13:36,000
Okay, we're going to jump!

260
00:13:36,000 --> 00:13:36,710
Jump?

261
00:13:41,210 --> 00:13:42,550
Run!

262
00:13:54,930 --> 00:13:56,600
The reserve power supply is in place!

263
00:13:56,600 --> 00:13:58,520
Reactor connection completed!

264
00:13:58,520 --> 00:13:59,810
Evacuate the flight deck!

265
00:13:59,810 --> 00:14:01,440
The deck is ready for Eva landing!

266
00:14:01,770 --> 00:14:03,780
All hands, prepare for impact!

267
00:14:03,780 --> 00:14:04,490
I can't believe this!

268
00:14:04,490 --> 00:14:07,400
Eva 02, landing on deck!

269
00:14:17,160 --> 00:14:18,750
What a waste!

270
00:14:18,750 --> 00:14:21,340
Target is approaching rapidly!

271
00:14:21,340 --> 00:14:23,500
It's coming! Port, 9 o'clock!

272
00:14:23,500 --> 00:14:24,760
Switching to external power!

273
00:14:28,590 --> 00:14:30,010
Switch completed.

274
00:14:31,260 --> 00:14:32,680
But we don't have any weapons.

275
00:14:32,680 --> 00:14:34,140
The prog knife will be more than enough.

276
00:14:42,980 --> 00:14:44,360
It's pretty big.

277
00:14:44,360 --> 00:14:45,570
That's what I figured!

278
00:14:47,780 --> 00:14:49,200
What are they going to do?!

279
00:14:49,200 --> 00:14:51,910
Hand-to-hand combat is the best way
to defeat Angels.

280
00:15:05,000 --> 00:15:06,710
Good work stopping it, Asuka!

281
00:15:06,710 --> 00:15:09,760
That's not funny! The flight deck is a mess!

282
00:15:16,770 --> 00:15:18,560
Hey, they fell!

283
00:15:18,560 --> 00:15:19,440
Asuka!

284
00:15:19,440 --> 00:15:22,100
It's impossible to fight underwater
with the type-B equipment!

285
00:15:22,100 --> 00:15:25,320
You never know unless you try!

286
00:15:43,630 --> 00:15:45,630
What a waste!

287
00:15:45,630 --> 00:15:46,800
How much cable is left?

288
00:15:48,130 --> 00:15:49,880
Another 1,200 meters!

289
00:15:49,880 --> 00:15:51,340
What are you going to do?

290
00:15:51,340 --> 00:15:52,340
We'll manage somehow.

291
00:15:53,260 --> 00:15:54,510
I've got to do something.

292
00:15:58,680 --> 00:16:01,230
The cable's going to run out!
Brace for the shock!

293
00:16:07,150 --> 00:16:08,440
Shoot!

294
00:16:08,440 --> 00:16:10,150
Eva lost the target!

295
00:16:10,150 --> 00:16:12,320
Now's the time to change disks...

296
00:16:14,030 --> 00:16:15,910
A Yak 38 Custom!

297
00:16:15,910 --> 00:16:17,830
Hey, Katsuragi!

298
00:16:17,830 --> 00:16:18,910
Kaji!

299
00:16:19,660 --> 00:16:22,210
I've got something to deliver,
so I'll be taking off now.

300
00:16:24,290 --> 00:16:25,500
Launch!

301
00:16:25,880 --> 00:16:28,840
Take care of the rest of this,
Captain Katsuragi.

302
00:16:31,010 --> 00:16:32,670
He ran away.

303
00:16:32,670 --> 00:16:35,010
The target is approaching Eva again!

304
00:16:35,760 --> 00:16:36,470
It's coming again!

305
00:16:37,470 --> 00:16:39,310
I'll finish it off this time.

306
00:16:42,890 --> 00:16:45,310
What?! It's not working!

307
00:16:45,310 --> 00:16:46,730
That's because this is B-type equipment.

308
00:16:46,730 --> 00:16:48,400
What're you going to do?!

309
00:16:48,400 --> 00:16:49,400
What am I supposed to do?

310
00:16:49,400 --> 00:16:52,400
You're pretty pitiful for being the Third Child!

311
00:16:52,400 --> 00:16:52,900
Here it comes!

312
00:16:57,620 --> 00:16:59,540
A mouth?!

313
00:16:59,540 --> 00:17:00,830
Well, it is an Angel.

314
00:17:03,710 --> 00:17:06,500
Eva 02 has entered the target's body.

315
00:17:06,500 --> 00:17:08,420
Doesn't that mean they've been eaten?

316
00:17:10,670 --> 00:17:12,880
It's practically like we're fishing!

317
00:17:12,880 --> 00:17:15,380
Fishing? Yes, fishing!

318
00:17:17,640 --> 00:17:19,510
We're right back in a pinch now.

319
00:17:19,510 --> 00:17:20,930
Shut up!

320
00:17:21,560 --> 00:17:24,100
Hey, get off me already, you pervert!

321
00:17:24,100 --> 00:17:26,140
But we've got to free ourselves somehow.

322
00:17:26,140 --> 00:17:27,730
Asuka, do you read me?

323
00:17:27,730 --> 00:17:29,360
Don't let go, no matter what!

324
00:17:30,770 --> 00:17:31,860
Captain...

325
00:17:31,860 --> 00:17:33,030
What?

326
00:17:33,030 --> 00:17:34,740
I'm requesting your cooperation.

327
00:17:36,700 --> 00:17:40,160
A point-blank assault by two
of the surviving battleships?!

328
00:17:40,160 --> 00:17:41,240
Correct.

329
00:17:41,240 --> 00:17:46,580
We'll scuttle two of the evacuated battleships
along the umbilical cable and set a trap.

330
00:17:47,000 --> 00:17:50,670
During that time, Eva 02 will open
the target's mouth,

331
00:17:50,670 --> 00:17:52,460
both ships will rush in,

332
00:17:52,460 --> 00:17:55,170
fire all of their bow turret cannons,

333
00:17:55,170 --> 00:17:58,090
and then self-destruct, destroying the target.

334
00:17:58,260 --> 00:17:59,970
That's absurd!

335
00:17:59,970 --> 00:18:03,140
Absurd, perhaps, but I don't think
it's impossible.

336
00:18:04,180 --> 00:18:05,390
I understand.

337
00:18:05,390 --> 00:18:08,850
All hands, abandon ship!
Repeat, all hands, abandon ship!

338
00:18:08,850 --> 00:18:11,820
All frigates, hurry and rescue the lifeboats!

339
00:18:12,270 --> 00:18:14,400
But what about the Eva?

340
00:18:14,400 --> 00:18:17,150
Not to worry. They'll be fine.

341
00:18:17,150 --> 00:18:20,700
Hey! Don't use Unit 02
without my permission!

342
00:18:21,120 --> 00:18:23,660
Do the two of you understand the operation?

343
00:18:23,660 --> 00:18:25,160
I'll do my best.

344
00:18:25,160 --> 00:18:26,040
I'm counting on you.

345
00:18:29,790 --> 00:18:33,960
Both ships have opened the Kingston valve!
Scuttling towards point Z.

346
00:18:33,960 --> 00:18:35,010
Roger!

347
00:18:35,010 --> 00:18:36,090
Cable reverse!

348
00:18:43,720 --> 00:18:45,270
Eva has started to surface!

349
00:18:45,270 --> 00:18:46,810
T-minus 70 to contact!

350
00:18:48,520 --> 00:18:51,900
Hey, how long are you going to stay there?
Get off me already!

351
00:18:51,900 --> 00:18:55,150
But we've got to pry open its mouth soon,
or we'll be killed too!

352
00:18:58,780 --> 00:19:00,660
T-minus 60 to contact.

353
00:19:00,660 --> 00:19:01,950
Status on the Angel's mouth?

354
00:19:01,490 --> 00:19:02,450
It's still not open!

355
00:19:05,080 --> 00:19:08,160
Both battleships are sinking
towards the target.

356
00:19:08,160 --> 00:19:10,750
Eva is continuing to surface,
T-minus 50 to contact.

357
00:19:10,750 --> 00:19:11,630
It's not working!

358
00:19:11,630 --> 00:19:13,040
There's no time left!

359
00:19:19,050 --> 00:19:21,010
Target has passed beneath the Tempest!

360
00:19:21,010 --> 00:19:22,300
Speed of ascent increasing!

361
00:19:22,300 --> 00:19:23,720
You're not going to make it! Hurry!

362
00:19:24,140 --> 00:19:25,970
Don't get any strange ideas.

363
00:19:25,970 --> 00:19:26,850
About what?

364
00:19:26,850 --> 00:19:29,310
Anyway, just focus your thoughts.

365
00:19:29,310 --> 00:19:29,890
I know!

366
00:19:35,480 --> 00:19:37,280
T-minus 20 to contact!

367
00:19:39,860 --> 00:19:42,070
T-minus 15 to contact!

368
00:19:42,070 --> 00:19:44,240
Open! Open! Open! Open!

369
00:19:44,240 --> 00:19:46,410
Open! Open! Open! Open!

370
00:19:57,920 --> 00:19:58,760
Fire!

371
00:20:16,900 --> 00:20:20,360
New Yokosuka (Old Odawara)

372
00:20:21,570 --> 00:20:23,410
You certainly went all-out.

373
00:20:23,410 --> 00:20:26,700
I should have anticipated
underwater combat.

374
00:20:26,990 --> 00:20:29,370
Oh, how rare. Remorse?

375
00:20:29,370 --> 00:20:32,960
Who cares? We collected valuable data too.

376
00:20:32,960 --> 00:20:33,920
That's true.

377
00:20:34,830 --> 00:20:36,080
Misato...

378
00:20:36,840 --> 00:20:38,340
This really is something special.

379
00:20:45,340 --> 00:20:46,890
They MATCH!

380
00:20:46,890 --> 00:20:48,850
I don't believe this!

381
00:20:48,850 --> 00:20:51,310
They broke their synchronization
ratio records, didn't they?

382
00:20:51,310 --> 00:20:54,480
For only seven seconds.
It must have been due to the danger.

383
00:20:55,810 --> 00:20:57,480
Hey, where's Mr. Kaji?

384
00:20:57,480 --> 00:21:01,400
He ran off. That idiot's got to be back
at headquarters by now!

385
00:21:02,780 --> 00:21:06,030
It was a pretty eventful trip.

386
00:21:06,570 --> 00:21:08,490
Was it caused by this, after all?

387
00:21:13,210 --> 00:21:15,920
It's already restored itself this far.

388
00:21:15,920 --> 00:21:20,250
It's frozen inside dura-bakelite,
but it's still alive.

389
00:21:20,250 --> 00:21:24,130
Without a doubt, this is the keystone of the
Human Instrumentality Project, isn't it?

390
00:21:24,130 --> 00:21:25,130
Correct.

391
00:21:25,130 --> 00:21:27,260
This is the first human being.

392
00:21:27,260 --> 00:21:28,180
Adam.

393
00:21:29,300 --> 00:21:34,100
She may have looked cute,
but she was a real bitch.

394
00:21:34,100 --> 00:21:37,060
Well, we won't have to see her again.

395
00:21:37,060 --> 00:21:39,770
Yeah, though ol' Mister Big Shot
has to see her at work.

396
00:21:39,770 --> 00:21:41,400
Man, I feel sorry for ya.

397
00:21:55,000 --> 00:21:58,460
My name is Asuka Langley Sohryu.
Nice to meet you.

398
00:21:58,500 --> 00:22:00,460
TO BE CONTINUED

399
00:23:05,900 --> 00:23:06,820
PREVIEW

400
00:23:07,280 --> 00:23:09,700
Asuka and Shinji, who are on completely
different wavelengths,

401
00:23:09,700 --> 00:23:11,870
are soundly beaten by an Angel.

402
00:23:11,870 --> 00:23:15,540
Aiming for perfect unison between the two,
Misato comes up with a plan.

403
00:23:15,540 --> 00:23:18,660
Next episode:
"Moment and Heart Together"

404
00:23:18,660 --> 00:23:20,960
I'll give you more fan service next time!

405
00:23:18,830 --> 00:23:20,870
MOMENT AND HEART TOGETHER
